# Demo GIFs are CI-only artifacts.  Tapes in assets/tapes/ are the
# source of truth; the demos workflow renders them and force-adds
# the result.  Local `make demos` writes to assets/demo-preview/
# instead (NEVER assets/demos/) so a contributor's local render
# can't dirty `git status` for the tracked CI-published file.  A
# repo guard fails any human commit that touches assets/demos/.
assets/demos/
assets/demo-preview/
# *.log (line 2) already covers .gif.log files captured by
# minimal_init.lua's :messages dump and read by the Makefile to
# detect post-render errors that vhs would otherwise hide inside
# the GIF (E-codes, "not modifiable", Lua stacks, etc.).

# luacov coverage artifacts (generated by `make test-cov`)
luacov.stats.out
luacov.report.out
